records.text_en:
ʿAbd al-Razzāq, from Maʿmar, from Qatāda, who said: "Saʿd ibn ʿUbāda got up to urinate and then came back and said: 'I feel something in my back.'" It was not long before he died. The jinn lamented him, saying (meter: *sarīʿ*):

"We killed the chief of the Khazraj, Saʿd ibn ʿUbāda;
We shot him with two arrows, and did not miss his heart."

